invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_avx2.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: broadcast_four drops the AND with the digit mask, which changes no
  digit, so every byte stays right. Without it clang 23 cannot show that a
  multiplier's bits from 32 up are zero, and multiplies by b's digits,
  and by the y's it carries from the last group, on two VPMULUDQs, two
  shifts and an add each. The script compiles the file for x86-64 with
  the pinned clang at both bounds and refuses a lane shifted left by 32.

--- old
    x[0] = lanes_broadcast(digits[0] & mask);
    x[1] = lanes_broadcast(digits[1] & mask);
    x[2] = lanes_broadcast(digits[2] & mask);
    x[3] = lanes_broadcast(digits[3] & mask);
--- new
    (void)mask;
    x[0] = lanes_broadcast(digits[0]);
    x[1] = lanes_broadcast(digits[1]);
    x[2] = lanes_broadcast(digits[2]);
    x[3] = lanes_broadcast(digits[3]);
